  state anywhere in the repo, and [38;5;153mindex.html[39m has no field that could carry a user ID.

  So the blocker is real: [1mthere is no source for [38;5;153muserId[39m at the only call site.[0m That has to be settled before the
  parameter has a meaning.

  [1mThe fork:[0m whether [38;5;153muserId[39m is data that arrives from outside the login call, or something login itself produces.

  - [1mUsername is the identifier[0m — [38;5;153mlogin[39m already receives and returns [38;5;153musername[39m; add the tracking log/return field using it
    and add no parameter. Free, nothing new to wire, no spoofing question. Costs you nothing later: if a real ID
