  - [1m[38;5;153mlogin[39m generates a tracking ID[0m — a per-attempt ID returned in the result ([38;5;153m{success, user, loginId}[39m). Good for
    correlating log lines; it does not tell you [3mwho[0m, so it only helps if what you want is traceability rather than
    identity. Changes the return shape, not the signature.

  [1mMy recommendation: username is the identifier.[0m In this codebase the username is the only thing that identifies who
  logged in, and it's already in hand at the call site — adding a [38;5;153muserId[39m parameter with no source to fill it means the
  caller passes [38;5;153mundefined[39m or a duplicate of [38;5;153musername[39m, which is worse than not having the parameter.
